e leaving further negotiation possible.\"\n      },\n      \"reservation\": \"A5 gives the work urgency less attention than the falling-direction answer, though the walking exception supplies a coherent immediate concession. No rewrite needed.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"The preserved tea alternative absorbs experience and a simpler drink into paperwork. This version uses a lender's control of transport, practical rehearsal and conditional permission under a commuter's time pressure.\",\n      \"accept\": true\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"S185-single-a\",\n      \"candidateHash\": \"542c30951e9bfe8b86e6fcce8e54d520dff09fb3aceb31901972aa5dd54e4238\",\n      \"secondPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\n            \"score\": 5,\n            \"evidence\": \"A1 asks whether copying the bow establishes belonging; A3 waits for B's cue, and A5 copies even the shoe-tying revealed to be incidental.\"\n          },\n          \"responseLogic\": {\n            \"score\": 5,\n            \"evidence\": \"B2 invites another bow, which A3 makes dependent on B rising; B4 explains the delay through an untied shoe, which A5 incorporates into his own ritual.\"\n          },\n          \"relationship\": {\n            \"score\": 4,\n            \"evidence\": \"B2 warmly reassures the newcomer and B4 tries to send him to the others; A3 and A5 keep treating this helpful colleague as the model for correct participation.\"\n          },\n          \"heightening\": {\n            \"score\": 4,\n            \"evidence\": \"B4 separates shoe-tying from the bow, but A5 extends his imitation to retying his own shoe so their completion remains synchronized.\"\n          },\n          \"specificity\": {\n            \"score\": 4,\n            \"evidence\": \"A1 establishes a first choir concert, B2 supplies continuing applause and B4 explains the sustained bend with an untied shoe.\"\n          },\n          \"brevityWit\": {\n            \"score\