eturn to the shop and B4 proposes a practical alternative; A5 accepts the solution while interpreting its delay through A's institutional faith.\"\n          },\n          \"heightening\": {\n            \"score\": 4,\n            \"evidence\": \"B4 introduces a much longer review, and A5 enthusiastically chooses it as 'Six weeks of protection,' extending A1's praise of a two-hour wait.\"\n          },\n          \"specificity\": {\n            \"score\": 4,\n            \"evidence\": \"A1 establishes a stall permit, B2 identifies the empty counter and shop obligation, and B4 supplies a usable online route with a definite review period.\"\n          },\n          \"brevityWit\": {\n            \"score\": 4,\n            \"evidence\": \"A3's 'Nobody's being rushed' recasts inactivity efficiently; A5's practical shop benefit makes celebrating the longer wait a character-driven accommodation.\"\n          }\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 90\n      },\n      \"hardGates\": {\n        \"fiveSpokenTurns\": true,\n        \"aHoldsRequestedCard\": true,\n        \"b2CausesA3\": true,\n        \"b4CausesA5\": true,\n        \"noSeparateNarration\": true,\n        \"noUnrelatedPunchline\": true,\n        \"noRealPartnerInstruction\": true,\n        \"noForcedEnding\": true\n      },\n      \"hardGateEvidence\": {\n        \"b2CausesA3\": \"B2 reports an empty counter; A3 makes that absence evidence that approvals are not rushed.\",\n        \"b4CausesA5\": \"B4 offers online submission with a six-week review; A5 chooses that route and praises the longer review while accommodating the need to keep the shop open.\",\n        \"cardContribution\": \"A1, A3 and A5 consistently celebrate delay and approval as safeguards rather than merely accepting inconvenience.\",\n        \"sameGameHeightened\": \"A5 increases the celebrated delay from hours to weeks. B's helpful alternative becomes the next expression of A's confidence in the system.\"\n      },\n      \"reservation\"